,"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in St. Croix County runs from 1951 to 2025, and January to February came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those 75 years. On the middle, 2025 had January to February at 44% of normal and October to November at 51%. So far in 2026, May to June sits at 60% of normal on the middle. Every grid had its driest year in 1976, with grid 29849 down to 53% of normal that year.</p>"}
